course: dictionary
lesson: 2703
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. «Digger» can mean a big machine, or a person or animal that digs. The context tells you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «The coloured paint marks show where pipes and cables run, so the diggers do not hit them.» The clues are pavement, pipes and cables, so a digger here is a machine. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence?
explain: «The Mole feels lively underground — he is a digger, and Badger's house suits him.» The clues are underground and the Mole, who is an animal. So a digger here is an animal that digs. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence.
fact: A digger is a large machine with a big metal bucket on an arm, used for digging holes and moving earth.
fact: A digger can also be a person or animal that digs, such as a mole, a rabbit or a wombat.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, «digger» is a friendly word for a soldier.
fact: Stay well away from moving diggers on building sites, because they are big and heavy.
fact: Phrases you may hear include a toy digger and a mechanical digger.
exercise: «The diggers do not hit the pipes, so workers mark them with paint.» What is a digger in this sentence? | A friendly word for a soldier | A pipe under the street | A rabbit in a field | *A large machine that moves earth
exercise: «The Mole feels lively underground — he is a digger.» What is a digger in this sentence? | *An animal that digs | A cable under the road | A soldier in Australia | A machine on a building site
exercise: In Australia, a friend calls you «digger». What does it mean? | *A friendly word for a soldier | A big metal bucket on an arm | A hole in the ground | A cable for the internet
test: In «A digger's engine drives a pump», which clue tells you the digger is a machine? | It is a friendly word | It has a name | *Its engine and pump | It is in the ground
test: Which sentence shows digger means an animal, not a machine? | «The workers spray paint before the roadworks.» | «Diggers check for cables before digging.» | *«The Mole feels lively underground — he is a digger.» | «A digger's tracks spread its weight.»
exam: When you meet the word «digger», what should you do to find its meaning? | *Read the clues around it, then try each meaning in the sentence | Look only at the word's length | Always pick the machine meaning, because it is the most common | Skip the word and never come back to it
